(def plus-page "(+ number more ...)\n\nAdds its arguments from left to right.\n\nOne argument returns it, and two call `add`.")
(def add-page "(add a b)\n\nReturns the sum of two numbers of one type.\n\nIt emits `a + b`. `+` takes one or more arguments.")
(def pi-page "pi\n\nHolds the ratio of a circle's circumference to its diameter, as an `f64`.\n\nIt emits `std::f64::consts::PI`.")
(def number-page "number\n\nMarks a type that does arithmetic.\n\nEvery integer and float type implements it, and `add`, `sub`, `mul`, `div`\nand `rem` take its types.")
(def eq-page "(eq a b)\n\nReturns whether two values are equal.\n\nIt borrows both values. `=` expands to it. `eq` is also a trait, Rust's\n`Eq`, which marks a type whose equality is total: the float types leave it\nout, and a key of a `hash-map` implements it.")
